+    // AA.3, in the user's words
+    'Model choice: an inexpensive capable tier for bounded, well-specified work; a stronger configured tier for uncertainty, difficult design, complex investigation, demanding review or a failed repair cycle. Neither the cheapest tier for every task nor a premium tier for every stage.',
+    'default escalation stays within the provider', 'needs `cross_provider: true` and a `permitted_for` scope',
+    'a same-named tier elsewhere never authorises a switch',
+    'After one repair cycle whose recheck still fails, the configured escalation runs as a new attempt before any equivalent repair',
+    'takes exactly the configured `on_exhaust` (`wait`, `ask` or a named `route`)',
+    'a more expensive binding no route names is never chosen', 'No provider switch is ever silent.',
+    // AA.4
+    '`identity_evidence` is `observed` (the provider\'s response), `host-reported`, `configured` (nothing reported), `unavailable` or `inconsistent` (both values kept).',
+    'provider metadata is attribution evidence, not cryptographic proof', 'missing pricing is unknown, never zero',
