+# Mock2 1.43.0: provider-scoped model tiers, agent workflow, attribution and delivery evidence
+
+Status: CANDIDATE, NOT PUBLISHED. Smoke-tested; publication waits for the developer's decision, after 1.42.0.
+Authorized by the developer on 2026-10-29 (`state/work.md`, Authorized scope: release-train lessons (1.42.0), then
+provider-scoped model tiers (1.43.0)). Baseline: the 1.42.0 candidate (`state/change-records/2026-10-30-lessons-2026-10-29.md`),
+itself on published 1.40.0. The 1.41.0 per-harness `fallback` setting never landed; `migrate` still converts a v1
+`fallback` field when one is present.
+
+## Why
+
+Agent routing named model releases in code (a built-in profile table, escalation to named models, provider guessed from
+model names), so every model release needed a Mock2 release, "a stronger model" meant nothing across providers, and
+attribution stopped at "requested vs actual (unknown when unreported)". This release keeps explicit provider selection,
+controllable spending, quality checks and truthful attribution while naming no model release in the standard.
+
+## What changes
+
+- **Contracts (new, installed under `.mock2/standards/`):** `Model-Routing.md` — qualified tiers `provider/tier`, the
+  registry (host-owned, versioned, `default_provider`, per-provider connections, tiers, role defaults, catalog, pricing),
+  precedence (job and session > environment > project > user > the registry's role default), statuses, discovery,
+  escalation, fallback and budgets, the execution record and identity evidence levels, the cost comparison;
+  `Work-Lifecycle.md` — the nine stages, distinguishable records, authorization bound to a plan revision, the queue's
+  waiting reasons, the event contract mapped onto Relay, the storytelling rules and a one-page walkthrough of the
+  illustrative "Track my support request" story. Schemas `schemas/model-registry.schema.json` and
+  `schemas/execution-record.v1.schema.json` (`mock2.execution/1`); non-normative samples: a two-provider registry with
+  placeholders, the compatibility registry `model-registry.legacy-1.40.json` (the 1.40.0 table as data, the only place
+  its model ids remain), and the story.
+- **Tool:** `orchestration-config.mjs`, `orchestrate.mjs` and `orchestration-adapters.mjs` resolve roles (now including
+  `release-helper`, which holds no promotion authority) to qualified tiers through the registry, in one resolution loop
+  that runs the bound route and every replacement (escalation, fallback, harness substitution, on-exhaust target)
+  through capability, retirement, native-harness, outage, budget, effort and price checks. Statuses: `planned`,
+  `planned-fallback`, `waiting`, `unqualified-tier`, `binding-missing`, `capability-mismatch`, `binding-retired`,
+  `unsupported`, `external-runner-required`, `disabled`. No silent provider or connection switch; a cross-provider move
+  only by a configured, permitted route, recorded. Unknown usage or price is unknown, never 0; totals per currency.
+  Pinned attempts and execution records; `migrate --scope S [--dry-run]`; `cost-compare`; `resolve --records`;
+  `--profile` kept one minor as a deprecated alias; `doctor` warns while a scope is on settings version 1 and when a
+  budget limit has no `on_exhaust`.
+- **Relay 1.3.0:** three schema-3 observations (`record.added`, `work.state.changed`, `execution.recorded`), minimum
+  reader 1.3.0, produced by `relay.mjs lifecycle` only when `relay.lifecycleEvidence` is on (off by default).
+- **Text:** PRO current §M.12 rewritten ("Role tier bindings and scoped controls") and new §AA (AA.1–AA.8), one line each
+  in §F, §I, §M.11, §P, §U, §R; `orchestration.md` rewritten around roles and tiers with the migration path; the
+  orchestration, run-ledger (optional `route` column), PRO, production-checklist and change-record rules; constitution;
+  entry block; the agents and build prompts; `.mock2/README.md`; capacity §16; the handoff and ledger templates.
+
+Compatibility: with no settings anywhere, routing goes through the compatibility registry and equals 1.40.0 exactly
+(the resolver and the native adapter output; a differential test of about 32,000 random version-1 cases against the
+1.40.0 tool: 0 mismatches). A version-1 file is never rewritten except by `migrate`, which keeps every effective route
+(600 random migrations: 0 differences, `--dry-run` writes nothing) and never copies a value only personal settings
+supplied into a project file. Behaviour change worth a release-note line: a version-1 pin that 1.40.0 refused as a
+provider/model mismatch now converts as written, since provider identity is no longer inferred from model names.
+
+No new gate: every refusal is the routing tool's own visible status.
+
+## Runs
+
+Coordinator plus background builders (routing code and contracts; standards text) in separate worktrees, on top of the
+1.42.0 candidate. Model attribution: not published. Independent review in a separate context: 3 HIGH (a budget route
+switching provider silently, a fallback skipping later checks, unknown usage costed as 0), 9 MEDIUM, 7 LOW, NITs; all
+fixed; confirmation rounds closed them and found one MEDIUM each (budget re-check after an on-exhaust hop; route-
+independent limits passed by an on-exhaust route), both fixed and confirmed closed. The last round left one NIT (below).
+
+## Checks
+
+Node 24.22.2, Python 3, Linux; no network and no paid call in any test (fakes only).
+
+- Generator: "v1.43.0 — 267 repo-template entries, 266 template identities, release.json covers 325 managed files"; a
+  second run changes nothing.
+- Final battery, full suite on the tested commit (`cand-1.43.0-r4`): 640 tests, 631 pass, 0 fail, 9 skipped. The
+  1.42.0 candidate: 574 tests, 565 pass, 0 fail, 9 skipped.
+- `secrets-coverage.mjs` 31/31; `install-binary.py` PASS; `relay-upgrade.py` PASS; outgoing secret scan against the
+  1.42.0 candidate: nothing found.
+- Release smoke against the candidate served locally, earlier release the 1.42.0 candidate served locally: 4 of 4 PASS
+  (machine install 325/325, repo-init 267/267, updater 1.42.0 → 1.43.0 with a project edit kept, hooks).
+- Not run: the Relay package's own tests and type check (no installed dependencies here); Windows and macOS smoke; the
+  names check with the private list.
+
+Docs consulted (2026-10-30): the Anthropic API reference for listing models and creating messages, read live — they
+match the requirement's section 3 (nullable `line` with "do not infer a line from the id"; `lifecycle`, `retires_at`;
+response `model`, `usage.service_tier` standard/priority/batch, `usage.speed`, `output_tokens_details.thinking_tokens`,
+cache fields, `server_tool_use`). The OpenAI references (models list, response retrieval, fast mode) could not be
+reached from the build environment; the OpenAI fields rest on the developer's reading of 2026-10-29. No SDK is pinned:
+Mock2's tool calls no provider API; hosts map provider usage with `usageFromResponse` (OpenAI `input_tokens` includes
+cached tokens and is reduced to uncached input; Anthropic's excludes cache reads and writes).
+
