+- Whether each native harness reports the worker's actual model per dispatch: until shown, its attribution is
+  `configured` or `unavailable`.
+- OpenAI documentation recheck from an environment that can reach it.
+- FOLLOW-UP NIT (review): when the bound tier's `settings_defaults` set `max_output_tokens`, a replacement route keeps
+  that value instead of its own default, so its own cap never relieves an output limit and the job waits (conservative:
+  it never exceeds a limit). Fix: carry over only explicitly configured settings in `routeAt`.
